# Code owners for release-critical and security-boundary paths.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: only paths that can publish artifacts, run with
# CI secrets, change what gets deployed, or move an auth/secret boundary. Broad
# application code is intentionally NOT owned here so day-to-day PRs stay
# unblocked. Generated, high-churn artifacts (root package.json, openapi.json,
# charts/agent-swarm/Chart.yaml) are excluded on purpose: owning them would gate
# roughly half of all PRs, mostly automated release bumps, for little security
# gain. As written this covers ~28% of recent merges.
#
# Ownership only becomes *enforced* when the `main` branch ruleset carries a
# pull request rule with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without it
# this file merely auto-requests review.
#
# Note: patterns are gitignore-style and the LAST matching pattern wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI / release surface — runs with repository secrets, publishes artifacts.
# Also covers this file, so ownership cannot be silently removed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                       @desplega-ai/admins
/scripts/                       @desplega-ai/admins

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Image + deploy surface — defines what actually ships and how it runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Dockerfile*                    @desplega-ai/admins
/apps/evals/Dockerfile          @desplega-ai/admins
/*-entrypoint.sh                @desplega-ai/admins
/docker-compose*                @desplega-ai/admins
/charts/                        @desplega-ai/admins
/deploy/                        @desplega-ai/admins

# Chart.yaml is deliberately left unowned (ownerless line = no owners, and the
# last matching pattern wins). It is generated by `bun run sync-chart-version`
# and its version/appVersion must match package.json — a mismatch already fails
# the Merge Gate. Owning it would gate every automated release bump for no real
# security gain, since chart *content* lives in templates/ and values.yaml,
# which stay owned above.
/charts/agent-swarm/Chart.yaml
/depot.json                     @desplega-ai/admins
/ecosystem.config.cjs           @desplega-ai/admins
/Makefile                       @desplega-ai/admins

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency / supply chain — registry config and resolved dependency graph.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/bunfig.toml                    @desplega-ai/admins
/bun.lock                       @desplega-ai/admins

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security boundaries — authorization, API key handling, secret redaction.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/rbac/                      @desplega-ai/admins
/src/utils/api-key.ts           @desplega-ai/admins
/src/utils/secret-scrubber.ts   @desplega-ai/admins
